<table>
<tr><th>Column</th><th>Data Type</th><th>Constraints</th><th>Description</th></tr>
<tr><td>id</td><td>INT</td><td>PRIMARY KEY, AUTO_INCREMENT</td><td>Auto-generated queue entry ID</td></tr>
<tr><td>token_number</td><td>INT</td><td>NOT NULL</td><td>Digital queue token number</td></tr>
<tr><td>student_id</td><td>VARCHAR(20)</td><td>DEFAULT NULL</td><td>Associated student</td></tr>
<tr><td>status</td><td>VARCHAR(20)</td><td>NOT NULL, DEFAULT 'Waiting'</td><td>Queue status (Waiting/Serving/Completed)</td></tr>
<tr><td>counter_number</td><td>INT</td><td>DEFAULT NULL</td><td>Service counter assignment</td></tr>
<tr><td>created_at</td><td>TIMESTAMP</td><td>DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP</td><td>Token generation timestamp</td></tr>
</table>

<h3>5.3.6 payment_deadlines Table</h3>
<table>
<tr><th>Column</th><th>Data Type</th><th>Constraints</th><th>Description</th></tr>
<tr><td>id</td><td>INT</td><td>PRIMARY KEY, AUTO_INCREMENT</td><td>Auto-generated deadline record ID</td></tr>
<tr><td>student_id</td><td>VARCHAR(20)</td><td>FOREIGN KEY REFERENCES students(student_id)</td><td>Associated student</td></tr>
<tr><td>fee_id</td><td>INT</td><td>FOREIGN KEY REFERENCES fees(id)</td><td>Associated fee item</td></tr>
<tr><td>due_date</td><td>DATE</td><td>NOT NULL</td><td>Payment due date</td></tr>
<tr><td>reminder_sent</td><td>BOOLEAN</td><td>DEFAULT FALSE</td><td>Whether reminder has been sent</td></tr>
<tr><td>reminder_count</td><td>INT</td><td>DEFAULT 0</td><td>Number of reminders sent</td></tr>
<tr><td>last_reminder_date</td><td>DATETIME</td><td>DEFAULT NULL</td><td>Date of last reminder</td></tr>
<tr><td>created_at</td><td>TIMESTAMP</td><td>DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP</td><td>Record creation timestamp</td></tr>
</table>

<h2>5.4 Entity Relationship Diagram</h2>
<p>The relationships between the database entities are as follows:</p>
<ul>
<li><b>Students to Fees:</b> One-to-Many. Each student can have multiple fee records (different fee types, terms). The fees table references students via student_id foreign key.</li>
<li><b>Students to Appointments:</b> One-to-Many. Each student can book multiple appointments over time. The appointments table references students via student_id foreign key.</li>
<li><b>Students to Queue:</b> One-to-Many. Each student can have multiple queue entries (different visits). The queue table references students via student_id.</li>
<li><b>Students to Payment Deadlines:</b> One-to-Many. Each student can have multiple payment deadlines for different fee items.</li>
<li><b>Fees to Payment Deadlines:</b> One-to-One (optional). Each fee item may have an associated payment deadline record linked via fee_id.</li>
</ul>

<h2>5.5 Input/Output Data Structures</h2>

<h3>5.5.1 PHP Database Connection</h3>
<p>The database connection is established in db.php using MySQLi procedural style:</p>
<pre>&lt;?php
$host = "localhost";
$user = "root";
$pass = "";
$dbname = "student_fees_db";
$conn = mysqli_connect($host, $user, $pass, $dbname);
if (!$conn) {
    die("Connection failed: " . mysqli_connect_error());
}
?&gt;</pre>

<h3>5.5.2 Student Data Query Pattern</h3>
<p>Student data is retrieved using parameterized SQL queries with JOINs to aggregate fee information:</p>
<pre>$sql = "SELECT s.*,
    COALESCE(SUM(f.amount), 0) AS total_fee,
    COALESCE(SUM(CASE WHEN f.status='Paid' THEN f.amount END),0) AS paid_amount,
    COALESCE(SUM(CASE WHEN f.status='Pending' THEN f.amount END),0) AS remaining_dues,
    (SELECT MIN(pd.due_date) FROM payment_deadlines pd
     INNER JOIN fees pf ON pd.fee_id = pf.id
     WHERE pd.student_id = s.student_id AND pf.status = 'Pending') AS next_due_date
FROM students s
LEFT JOIN fees f ON s.student_id = f.student_id
GROUP BY s.student_id
ORDER BY s.class_name, s.name LIMIT 30";</pre>

<h3>5.5.3 Analytics Query Pattern</h3>
<p>The analytics module uses aggregate queries with GROUP BY for fee type breakdown:</p>
<pre>$stats_sql = "SELECT 
    fee_type, 
    SUM(CASE WHEN status = 'Paid' THEN amount ELSE 0 END) as collected,
    SUM(CASE WHEN status = 'Pending' THEN amount ELSE 0 END) as pending,
    COUNT(CASE WHEN status = 'Paid' THEN 1 END) as paid_count,
    COUNT(CASE WHEN status = 'Pending' THEN 1 END) as pending_count,
    COUNT(id) as total_records
    FROM fees 
    GROUP BY fee_type";</pre>

<h3>5.5.4 Firebase Firestore Data Structure</h3>
<p>Firestore collections used in the system:</p>
<ul>
<li><b>students:</b> Collection storing student profile documents with fields: student_id, name, photo_url, course</li>
<li><b>notifications:</b> Collection storing real-time notification documents with fields: student_id, title, message, status, timestamp</li>
<li><b>messages:</b> Collection storing student messages with fields: student_id, content, timestamp</li>
</ul>

