<h1>CHAPTER 6: MODULE DESIGN SPECIFICATIONS</h1>

<h2>6.1 Introduction</h2>
<p>This chapter provides detailed design specifications for each module of the FeeFlow system, including pseudo-code, algorithms, variable dictionaries, and functionality descriptions.</p>

<h2>6.2 Admin Module Design</h2>

<h3>6.2.1 Authentication Submodule (admin/auth.php)</h3>
<p><b>Purpose:</b> Restrict access to admin pages to authenticated users only.</p>
<p><b>Algorithm:</b></p>
<pre>1. Start PHP session (session_start())
2. Check if $_SESSION['admin_logged_in'] is set and equals true
3. IF not authenticated:
   a. Redirect to login.php
   b. Call exit()
4. ELSE: Allow page content to render</pre>

<h3>6.2.2 Student Management Submodule (admin/students_list.php)</h3>
<p><b>Purpose:</b> Display, search, filter, and delete student records.</p>
<p><b>Key Functions:</b></p>
<ul>
<li><b>filterTable():</b> JavaScript function that filters displayed rows based on search input, class, gender, and status dropdown values. Matches data-name, data-id, and data-email attributes against search text.</li>
<li><b>confirmDelete(id, name):</b> JavaScript function that opens a confirmation modal with student name and ID, then sets the delete confirmation link to students_list.php?delete=ID.</li>
<li><b>exportCSV():</b> JavaScript function that collects visible table row data, formats as CSV, creates a Blob, and triggers browser download.</li>
</ul>
<p><b>Variable Dictionary:</b></p>
<table>
<tr><th>Variable</th><th>Type</th><th>Description</th></tr>
<tr><td>$stats</td><td>Array</td><td>Student count statistics (total, active, inactive, suspended)</td></tr>
<tr><td>$fee_stats</td><td>Array</td><td>Aggregate fee statistics (total_paid, total_pending)</td></tr>
<tr><td>$students</td><td>Array</td><td>Array of student records with fee aggregations</td></tr>
<tr><td>$class_order</td><td>Array</td><td>Ordered list of class names for sorting</td></tr>
</table>

<h3>6.2.3 Payment Monitoring Submodule (admin/online_payments.php)</h3>
<p><b>Purpose:</b> Monitor and manage online payment transactions.</p>
<p><b>Functionality:</b></p>
<ul>
<li>Displays summary statistics cards (today's payments, total transactions, completed amount, pending amount)</li>
<li>Filter tabs for viewing all, today, pending, or completed payments</li>
<li>Transaction table with receipt number, student details, amount, payment method, status, date, and action buttons</li>
<li>Payment method badges use color-coded CSS classes (mobile, card, bank, ussd, autopay)</li>
</ul>

<h2>6.3 Student Module Design</h2>

<h3>6.3.1 Student Dashboard Submodule (student/dashboard.php)</h3>
<p><b>Purpose:</b> Provide personalized dashboard with fee overview and quick actions.</p>
<p><b>Algorithm:</b></p>
<pre>1. Include database connection and student header
2. Get student_id from GET parameter (default: S101)
3. Query students table for student details
4. IF student not found: Display error message and exit
5. Query fees table for:
   a. Total paid amount (SUM with status='Paid')
   b. Total pending amount (SUM with status='Pending')
   c. Full fee history (ORDER BY created_at DESC)
   d. Fee breakdown by type
   e. Overdue count and amount (JOIN with payment_deadlines)
6. Render dashboard layout:
   a. Welcome section with student name and ID
   b. Overdue payment alert (if applicable)
   c. Quick Access Menu with 6 navigation cards
   d. Stat cards (Total Paid, Total Pending, Financial Clearance)
   e. Fee breakdown sidebar with recent notifications
   f. Payment history table with action buttons
   g. Profile modal
7. Initialize Firebase Firestore listeners for real-time notifications</pre>

<h3>6.3.2 Online Payment Gateway Submodule (student/payment_gateway.php)</h3>
<p><b>Purpose:</b> Provide secure payment interface for settling pending fees.</p>
<p><b>Payment Methods Supported:</b></p>
<ol>
<li><b>Credit/Debit Card:</b> Form with card number, expiry date, CVV fields. Assumes PCI-compliant processing through third-party gateway.</li>
<li><b>Mobile Money:</b> Form with phone number and provider selection (MTN, MTN, M-Pesa). Simulates mobile money payment initiation.</li>
<li><b>Bank Transfer:</b> Displays bank account details for manual transfer. No form submission; provides reference information.</li>
</ol>

<h3>6.3.3 Appointment Booking Submodule (student/book_appointment.php)</h3>
<p><b>Purpose:</b> Allow students to book appointments with the finance office.</p>
<p><b>Algorithm:</b></p>
<pre>1. Get student_id and fetch student details
2. Fetch upcoming appointments for this student
3. IF form submitted (POST):
   a. Validate appointment_date (between tomorrow and +30 days)
   b. Validate appointment_time (available time slot)
   c. Check slot capacity (max 5 appointments per time slot)
   d. IF slot available: INSERT into appointments table
   e. ELSE: Display error message "Time slot full"
4. Render booking interface:
   a. Hero section with appointment info
   b. Outstanding balance alert (if applicable)
   c. Upcoming appointments list
   d. Appointment form with date picker, time slot grid, purpose dropdown
   e. Appointment tips section
5. Time slots: 30-minute intervals from 08:00 to 15:00 (14 slots total)</pre>
<p><b>Available Time Slots:</b></p>
<pre>$times = ['08:00','08:30','09:00','09:30','10:00','10:30',
          '11:00','11:30','12:00','13:00','13:30','14:00','14:30','15:00'];</pre>

<h2>6.4 Payment Processing Module</h2>

<h3>6.4.1 Payment Plan Management (student/payment_plans.php)</h3>
<p><b>Purpose:</b> Offer flexible installment payment options to students.</p>
<p><b>Available Plans:</b></p>
<table>
<tr><th>Plan Name</th><th>Duration</th><th>Installments</th><th>Monthly Amount</th></tr>
<tr><td>Standard Plan</td><td>3 months</td><td>3 equal payments</td><td>Total Pending / 3</td></tr>
<tr><td>Extended Plan</td><td>6 months</td><td>6 equal payments</td><td>Total Pending / 6</td></tr>
<tr><td>Quick Pay</td><td>2 months</td><td>2 equal payments</td><td>Total Pending / 2</td></tr>
</table>

<h3>6.4.2 Payment Receipt Generation (student/payment_receipt.php)</h3>
<p><b>Purpose:</b> Display payment confirmation receipt with print capability.</p>
<p><b>Receipt Layout:</b></p>
<ul>
<li>Green gradient header with success icon and "Payment Successful!" message</li>
<li>Receipt number and timestamp</li>
<li>Student information grid (name, ID, class, payment method)</li>
<li>Amount paid display (UGX and USD)</li>
<li>Fee items covered list</li>
<li>Transaction reference (if bank transfer)</li>
<li>"What's Next" section with follow-up steps</li>
<li>Print and navigation buttons</li>
</ul>
<p><b>Print CSS:</b> The receipt uses @media print rules to hide all page elements except the receipt content:</p>
<pre>@media print {
    body * { visibility: hidden; }
    .receipt-container, .receipt-container * { visibility: visible; }
    .receipt-container { position: absolute; left: 0; top: 0; width: 100%; }
    .no-print { display: none; }
}</pre>

<h2>6.5 Queue Management Module (student/queue.php)</h2>
<p><b>Purpose:</b> Display live queue status for the finance office.</p>
<p><b>Algorithm:</b></p>
<pre>1. Query queue table for currently serving token:
   "SELECT token_number, counter_number FROM queue WHERE status = 'Serving' LIMIT 1"
2. Query queue table for waiting count:
   "SELECT COUNT(*) as waiting_count FROM queue WHERE status = 'Waiting'"
3. Calculate estimated wait time: waiting_count * 5 minutes
4. Query full queue list sorted by status (Serving first) then token number
5. Render:
   a. Currently serving panel with token number, counter, wait time
   b. Join queue promotion card
   c. Queue overview table with token, student ID, status badges
   d. Tip box for long wait times</pre>

<h2>6.6 Payment Reminders Module</h2>

<h3>6.6.1 Admin Reminder System (admin/send_reminders.php)</h3>
<p><b>Purpose:</b> Send batch payment reminders to overdue students.</p>
<p><b>Algorithm:</b></p>
<pre>1. Display summary statistics (students overdue, overdue fees count, total overdue amount)
2. Provide form with overdue period dropdown (0, 7, 14, 30 days)
3. On form submission:
   a. UPDATE payment_deadlines SET reminder_sent=TRUE, 
      reminder_count = reminder_count + 1, 
      last_reminder_date = NOW()
   b. WHERE due_date < CURDATE() - INTERVAL days_overdue DAY
   c. AND fee status = 'Pending'
4. Display success message with affected student count
5. Show overdue students list with names, IDs, emails, amounts</pre>

<h3>6.6.2 Student Reminder View (student/payment_reminders.php)</h3>
<p><b>Purpose:</b> Display overdue and upcoming payment deadlines to students.</p>
<p><b>Layout:</b></p>
<ul>
<li>Left column: Overdue Payments (red theme) showing overdue fee items with days overdue count and reminder history</li>
<li>Right column: Upcoming Deadlines (amber theme) showing pending fees with days remaining</li>
<li>Each item has a direct "Pay Now" or "Pay Before Deadline" button</li>
</ul>

<h2>6.7 Analytics and Reporting Module (admin/payment_analytics.php)</h2>
<p><b>Purpose:</b> Provide comprehensive financial analytics and reporting.</p>
<p><b>Components:</b></p>
<ol>
<li><b>KPI Cards:</b> Total Collections, Outstanding Balance, Recovery Rate (percentage), Total Ledger</li>
<li><b>Collection by Fee Type Table:</b> Each fee type with collected amount, pending amount, visual progress bar and percentage</li>
<li><b>Payment Method Distribution:</b> Horizontal bar chart showing payment method popularity with counts and percentages</li>
<li><b>Top Outstanding Students:</b> Table of students with highest pending amounts, color-coded by severity (Critical > $5000, High > $2000, Moderate > $0)</li>
<li><b>Key Performance Metrics:</b> Average payment per transaction, average outstanding per student, students with perfect payment record</li>
<li><b>Report Generation:</b> Buttons for CSV, PDF, Excel, and Email summary export (UI placeholders)</li>
</ol>

