<h1>CHAPTER 7: SYSTEM VERIFICATION</h1>

<h2>7.1 Introduction</h2>
<p>This chapter presents the testing and verification methodology used to validate the FeeFlow system. It covers unit testing, integration testing, user acceptance testing, and the results of testing activities.</p>

<h2>7.2 Testing Strategy</h2>
<p>The testing strategy for FeeFlow followed a multi-level approach:</p>
<ol>
<li><b>Unit Testing:</b> Individual PHP scripts and functions were tested independently to verify correct output.</li>
<li><b>Integration Testing:</b> Module interactions were tested, particularly database query execution and data flow between pages.</li>
<li><b>User Acceptance Testing:</b> Simulated user scenarios were executed to validate that the system meets functional requirements.</li>
<li><b>Database Testing:</b> SQL queries were validated for correct syntax and expected results using seed data.</li>
</ol>

<h2>7.3 Unit Testing</h2>

<h3>7.3.1 Database Connection Test</h3>
